    },
    {
      "id": "l-u",
      "bn": "উ",
      "tr": "u",
      "en": "u as in 'food' (short-u letter)",
      "pos": "letter",
      "lesson": "s01-l02",
      "notes": "Name: hroshsho-u (হ্রস্ব উ). Sounds the same as ঊ in modern speech."
    },
    {
      "id": "l-uu",
      "bn": "ঊ",
      "tr": "u",
      "en": "u as in 'food' (long-u letter)",
      "pos": "letter",
      "lesson": "s01-l02",
      "notes": "Name: dirgho-u (দীর্ঘ ঊ). Same sound as উ; it is উ with an extra loop on top-right. Rare at the start of words."
    },
    {
      "id": "l-ri",
      "bn": "ঋ",
      "tr": "ri",
      "en": "ri as in 'rip'",
      "pos": "letter",
      "lesson": "s01-l02",
      "notes": "Name: ri (ঋ). Historically a vowel; in modern Bengali it is simply said 'ri'. Found mostly in Sanskrit-origin words."
    },
    {
      "id": "l-e",
      "bn": "এ",
      "tr": "e",
      "en": "e as in 'bed' or 'ay' as in 'say'",
      "pos": "letter",
      "lesson": "s01-l02",
      "notes": "Name: e (এ). Two pronunciations; the word decides which (open æ in এক 'ack' and এখন 'ækhon'; 'ay' in এই 'ei')."
    },
