      "en": "season",
      "pos": "noun",
      "lesson": "s01-l02",
      "notes": "Bengal traditionally has six seasons (ছয় ঋতু)."
    },
    {
      "id": "ek",
      "bn": "এক",
      "tr": "ek",
      "en": "one",
      "pos": "number",
      "lesson": "s01-l02",
      "notes": "Pronounced like English 'ack' (open e)."
    },
    {
      "id": "ekhon",
      "bn": "এখন",
      "tr": "ekhon",
      "en": "now",
      "pos": "adv",
      "lesson": "s01-l02",
      "notes": "Pronounced with an open e, like 'ack-hon' (æ)."
    },
    {
      "id": "l-oi",
      "bn": "ঐ",
      "tr": "oi",
      "en": "oi as in 'boy'",
      "pos": "letter",
      "lesson": "s01-l03",
      "notes": "Name: oi (ঐ). Looks like এ with an extra flick on top. As a word, ঐ means 'that (over there)', today usually spelled ওই."
    },
    {
      "id": "l-o2",
      "bn": "ও",
      "tr": "o",
      "en": "o as in 'go'",
      "pos": "letter",
      "lesson": "s01-l03",
      "notes": "Name: o (ও). Rounder, closed 'o', unlike the short open অ. As a word, ও also means 'and / also' or 's/he'."
    },
    {
      "id": "l-ou",
      "bn": "ঔ",
      "tr": "ou",
      "en": "ou as in 'low'",
      "pos": "letter",
      "lesson": "s01-l03",
      "notes": "Name: ou (ঔ). It is ও with an extra squiggle on top. Rare; mostly in formal/Sanskrit-origin words."
    },
    {
      "id": "oikko",
      "bn": "ঐক্য",
      "tr": "oikko",
      "en": "unity",
      "pos": "noun",
      "lesson": "s01-l03",
      "notes": "The ক্য cluster doubles the k sound: oik-ko."
    },
    {
      "id": "oitijjho",
      "bn": "ঐতিহ্য",
      "tr": "oitijjho",
      "en": "heritage / tradition",
      "pos": "noun",
      "lesson": "s01-l03",
      "notes": "The হ্য cluster is said like a doubled \"jjh\": oi-tij-jho."
    },
